        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "8f7b43e300bc478ebd50ba995d62d4c7c9fcfef6",
            "parents": [
                "7354b21b73293d510d44cfda756add69a009c7ba"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/42/80242/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "createdOn": 1751163668,
            "author": {
                "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "An example configuration could be useful here, to clarify how to\ndecompose something like\n\n```\n/dev/serial/by-path/platform-fd500000.pcie-pci-0000:01:00.0-usb-0:1.1:1.0-port0\n/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Serial-if00-port0\n```\n\ninto the properties defined in the schema.\n\n\nIt would be great if that was also possible by just reading the schema without going through the commit message.\n\nEssentially, if i have a serial device (like ```/dev/serial/...```)\nhow do i map that information to the configuration schema."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I would let maintainers comment if they are fine with adding linux specific details (such as path details) into the schema properties descriptions. If they are fine with it, i will go ahead and add it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/usb_port.json",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "On line 4 it is \"USB Port\" and in the file name as well,\nbut the description says it's a \"serial port\".\n\nIs it a serial port exposed via a USB interface?\n\nIf that's the case, maybe we should adjust the name of this schema, Type and filename to match.\n\nSomething like\n```USBSerialPort``` ?\n\n\nHowever modbus serial line protocol does not require a USB device, right?\n\nMaybe it can just be\n```\nSerialPort\n```\nor\n```\nModbusSerialPort\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/usb_port.json",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> On line 4 it is \"USB Port\" and in the file name as well,\n> but the description says it's a \"serial port\".\n\nChanged the description to reflect USB.\n\n> \n> Is it a serial port exposed via a USB interface?\n\nAll USB (Universal Serial Bus) ports are serial.\n\n> \n> If that's the case, maybe we should adjust the name of this schema, Type and filename to match.\n> \n> Something like\n> ```USBSerialPort``` ?\n\nUSB - Universal Serial Bus, so adding Serial makes it redundant, hence i didn't add it.\n\n> \n> \n> However modbus serial line protocol does not require a USB device, right?\n> \n> Maybe it can just be\n> ```\n> SerialPort\n> ```\n> or\n> ```\n> ModbusSerialPort\n> ```\n\nHere i am specifically modeling a USB port as properties of USB ports are being mentioned. For other type of serial ports a different schema definition can be added as per need in future."
                }
            ],
